  "2026-11-05T14:29:51.164Z",codex-agent,"Full npm release validation remains active at unchanged thresholds with two workers. Current ordered output contains 711 passing reports and one failure in the existing erasure-accountability competing-purger test (each child has an unchanged 30-second deadline). The detailed failure is pending the suite summary; no infrastructure classification or passing release certificate is claimed. Remaining test processes continue executing and producing coverage data. Retain the complete run, inspect its terminal diagnostics, then verify the failed case on retry or in the subsequent Bun gate before disposition. The SDK optional-schema loader used for digest folder resolution was also inspected and performs source reads with no created paths."
  "2026-11-05T16:29:22.119Z",codex-agent,"The full npm command completed with exit 1 after 16315 seconds. Ordinary suite: 2586 tests, 2585 passed, 1 failed, 0 cancelled/skipped/todo. Exact failure: test/erasure-accountability.test.ts, one tracker serializes a competing purger at EVERY accountability boundary and reports peer success, reached the configured VerificationRefusal erasure/time_ms work bound. It was not a child-process assertion timeout. No verification budget or gate threshold was changed. The runner correctly stopped before its serial batch and later release stages, so incomplete whole-source coverage is not a certificate. All three new round-4 regressions and the 500-sequence admission model passed; changed production modules, including record-format, repo, tracker admission, worktree and shared stat-cache, measured 100 in every coverage dimension. The subsequent full Bun gate is now running with the same two-worker isolation and will independently rerun the bounded erasure case."
  "2026-11-05T16:47:36.489Z",codex-agent,"Retry receipt: the exact erasure-accountability competing-purger test that reached the erasure/time_ms bound in npm passed during the subsequent full Bun gate in 164454 ms, with unchanged verification budgets, assertions and two-worker isolation. The earlier npm run took 316328 ms in that case and hit the configured work bound under observed host load. This satisfies the requested retry condition for the local timeout; the full npm command still exited 1 and its serial batch did not run, so that command is not relabelled as an all-green full gate. The full Bun gate remains active with no reported failures and will supply the complete release/coverage verdict."
